; SPDX-FileCopyrightText: © 2026 Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
; SPDX-License: MPL-2.0
; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
;
; K9 Coordination File Grammar, v1.3.0
; Normative for parsing coordination.k9 files
; Prose specification: ../COORDINATION-K9-SPEC.adoc
;
; K9 is YAML-like but NOT standard YAML. It is a domain-specific
; coordination language with strict schema validation.
;
; Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive string literals).
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.2.0 -> v1.3.0), owner rulings by selector, 2026-11-20
; (K9 worker reach, Q4 and Q6 to Q12):
;   - One optional section, additive and last: reach (after
;     coordination). Every string the v1.2.0 grammar derives, the
;     v1.3.0 grammar derives; no v1.2.0 rule changes except body,
;     which gains the one optional element.
;   - reach is the worker reach contract: which repos and actions each
;     agent role may use, and the role's limits (temporal window,
;     breadth and depth, time to live, rate, breach mode). The hub and
;     the reach hook honour it only in metadatastician/standards
;     (spec rule 18).
;   - indent5 (10 spaces) and indent6 (12 spaces) for the nesting
;     inside reach.
;   - Schema rules the grammar cannot express are spec rules 15 to 23,
;     enforced by tools/validate.
;
; LINE-LENGTH CONSTRAINT (normative; owner ruling I4, 2026-11-12):
;   No line of a k9-file is longer than 998 octets, not counting the
;   line-end (CR and LF) that closes it. A file with a longer line does
;   not conform even if it matches k9-file below. ABNF has no compact
;   way to bound a line, so the constraint is stated here and enforced
;   by the validator (spec "Validation Rules", rule 14). It is the
;   RFC 5322 Section 2.1.1 bound and makes the registered "8bit"
;   encoding label exact. The rules below are unchanged by it.
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.1.1 -> v1.2.0), owner ruling 2026-10-13:
;   - Two optional sections, additive: every string the v1.1.1 grammar
;     derives, the v1.2.0 grammar derives. Since 2026-11-12 the
;     998-octet line constraint above also applies, so a v1.1.1 file
;     with a longer line is not a conforming v1.2.0 file.
;     build_commands (after project): the commands an agent may run,
;     each with its purpose. innervation (after architecture): the
;     signals the repo emits (afferent), responds to (efferent) and the
;     local guards it enforces (reflex).
;   - indent4 (8 spaces) for the consumer lists inside innervation.
;   - Comments are ASCII, as RFC 5234 requires, apart from the SPDX
;     copyright line (the earlier files also carried
;     non-ASCII arrows and comparison signs).
;   - Editorial, 2026-11-09 (the language is unchanged):
;     * deed-filename is right-recursive. As 1*(... / ".") %s".deed",
;       a greedy repetition also consumed ".deed", so no deed_ref ever
;       validated under apg-js. The new form denotes the same strings:
;       one or more name characters, then ".deed" (proved in
;       tools/validate/proofs/GrammarExtension.idr).
;     * `date` lists iso8601-datetime first. RFC 5234 alternation is
;       unordered, but ordered-choice parsers such as apg-js take the
;       first alternative that matches, and the calendar-date prefix of
;       a date-time matched first, so no date-time was ever accepted
;       (spec rule 10).
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.1.0 -> v1.1.1), owner rulings D317 + D318:
;   - lang-list items are indented one level under "languages:" (indent2),
;     the same nesting every other list follows (was: indent, a defect)
;   - Full-line "#" comments are permitted between sections (rule gap);
;     still not within a section; "---" separators remain invalid
;
; CHANGELOG (v1.0.0 -> v1.1.0):
;   - Added %s prefix for case-sensitive literals (RFC 7405)
;   - Unified line endings to line-end (CRLF or LF) throughout
;   - Added blank-line support between sections
;   - Added bare-version to value rule (unquoted 1.0.0 etc.)
;   - Expanded iso8601-datetime to full RFC 3339 (frac-sec, tz offsets)
;   - Added escape sequences to strings (\" \\ \n \t)
;   - Added indent2 / indent3 aliases for nested indentation
;   - Expanded glob-pattern with ?, [], {}
;   - Required >=1 entry in ecosystem / coordination sections
;   - Fixed optional sections: explicit order, no duplicates

k9-file       = magic-line line-end header *gap body

; --- Magic Number (REQUIRED first line) ----------------------------
magic-line    = %s"K9!"

; --- SPDX Header (REQUIRED) ----------------------------------------
header        = 1*spdx-line
spdx-line     = "#" SP %s"SPDX-" 1*text-char line-end

; --- Gaps between sections (not permitted within a section) --------
; A gap is a blank line or a full-line comment starting in column 0.
gap           = blank-line / comment-line
blank-line    = *SP line-end
comment-line  = "#" *text-char line-end

; --- Body Structure ------------------------------------------------
; Required sections MUST appear in this order.
; Optional sections MUST appear in the order shown; each at most once.
body          = metadata-section    *gap
                project-section     *gap
                [build-commands-section *gap]
                invariants-section  *gap
                [protected-section     *gap]
                [architecture-section  *gap]
                [innervation-section   *gap]
                [do-not-create-section *gap]
                [terminology-section   *gap]
                [ecosystem-section     *gap]
                [coordination-section  *gap]
                [reach-section         *gap]

; --- Required Sections ---------------------------------------------

metadata-section = %s"metadata:" line-end
                   1*metadata-field

metadata-field = indent %s"schema:"         SP value line-end
               / indent %s"schema_version:" SP value line-end
               / indent %s"generated_by:"   SP value line-end
               / indent %s"last_updated:"   SP date  line-end

project-section = %s"project:" line-end
                  1*project-field

project-field  = indent %s"name:"         SP string        line-end
               / indent %s"description:"  SP string        line-end
               / indent %s"license:"      SP spdx-id       line-end
               / indent %s"repo:"         SP repo-path     line-end
               / indent %s"deed_ref:"     SP deed-filename line-end
               / indent %s"languages:"    line-end lang-list
               / indent %s"build_system:" SP symbol        line-end
               / indent %s"runtime:"      SP symbol        line-end

lang-list      = 1*(indent2 "- " symbol line-end)

invariants-section = %s"invariants:" line-end
                     *invariant-entry                     ; May be empty

invariant-entry = indent  "- " %s"id:"       SP symbol   line-end
                  indent2      %s"rule:"     SP string   line-end
                  indent2      %s"reason:"   SP string   line-end
                  [indent2     %s"severity:" SP severity line-end]

severity       = %s"critical" / %s"high" / %s"moderate"

; --- Optional Sections ---------------------------------------------

build-commands-section = %s"build_commands:" line-end
                         1*build-command-entry

build-command-entry = indent  "- " %s"command:" SP string line-end
                      indent2      %s"purpose:" SP string line-end

protected-section = %s"protected:" line-end
                    1*protected-entry

protected-entry = indent  "- " %s"path:"   SP file-path line-end
                  indent2      %s"reason:" SP string    line-end

architecture-section = %s"architecture:" line-end
                       1*arch-entry

arch-entry     = indent  "- " %s"id:"                  SP symbol line-end
                 indent2      %s"decision:"            SP string line-end
                 indent2      %s"reason:"              SP string line-end
                 [indent2     %s"alternatives_rejected:" line-end alt-list]

alt-list       = 1*(indent3 "- " string line-end)

innervation-section = %s"innervation:" line-end
                      1*innervation-entry          ; >=1 required

innervation-entry = indent %s"afferent:" line-end afferent-list
                  / indent %s"efferent:" line-end efferent-list
                  / indent %s"reflex:"   line-end reflex-list

; Afferent: a signal this repo emits, and who consumes it.
afferent-list  = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"signal:"      SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"description:" SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"triggers_on:" SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"consumers:"   line-end consumer-list)

consumer-list  = 1*(indent4 "- " symbol line-end)

; Efferent: a signal this repo responds to, and whether it fixes itself.
efferent-list  = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"signal:"   SP string  line-end
                    indent3      %s"action:"   SP string  line-end
                    indent3      %s"auto_fix:" SP boolean line-end)

; Reflex: a local guard that needs no central processing.
reflex-list    = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"trigger:" SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"guard:"   SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"action:"  SP string line-end)

boolean        = %s"true" / %s"false"

do-not-create-section = %s"do_not_create:" line-end
                        1*dnc-entry

dnc-entry      = indent  "- " %s"pattern:"     SP glob-pattern line-end
                 indent2      %s"reason:"      SP string       line-end
               / indent  "- " %s"description:" SP string       line-end
                 indent2      %s"reason:"      SP string       line-end

terminology-section = %s"terminology:" line-end
                      1*term-entry

term-entry     = indent  "- " %s"correct:"   SP symbol line-end
                 indent2      %s"incorrect:" line-end incorrect-list
                 [indent2     %s"context:"   SP string line-end]

incorrect-list = 1*(indent3 "- " symbol line-end)

ecosystem-section = %s"ecosystem:" line-end
                    1*ecosystem-entry               ; >=1 required

ecosystem-entry = indent %s"depends_on:"  line-end dep-list
                / indent %s"consumed_by:" line-end dep-list
                / indent %s"related:"     line-end dep-list

dep-list       = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"name:" SP symbol line-end
                    indent3      %s"role:" SP string line-end)

coordination-section = %s"coordination:" line-end
                       1*coordination-entry          ; >=1 required

coordination-entry = indent %s"active:"    line-end active-list
                   / indent %s"completed:" line-end completed-list
                   / indent %s"available:" line-end available-list

active-list    = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"agent:"   SP symbol line-end
                    indent3      %s"area:"    SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"started:" SP date   line-end
                    indent3      %s"status:"  SP status line-end
                    [indent3     %s"blocker:" SP string line-end])

completed-list = 1*(indent2 "- " %s"agent:"     SP symbol line-end
                    indent3      %s"area:"      SP string line-end
                    indent3      %s"completed:" SP date   line-end)

available-list = 1*(indent2 "- " string line-end)

status         = %s"in-progress" / %s"blocked" / %s"paused"

; --- Reach (v1.3.0) ------------------------------------------------
; The worker reach contract. Fields appear in the order shown.

reach-section  = %s"reach:" line-end
                 indent  %s"contract_id:"  SP symbol    line-end
                 indent  %s"serial:"       SP 1*DIGIT   line-end
                 [indent %s"supersedes:"   SP string    line-end]
                 indent  %s"valid_from:"   SP date      line-end
                 indent  %s"expires:"      SP date      line-end
                 indent  %s"default:"      SP %s"deny"  line-end
                 indent  %s"approved_by:"  SP symbol    line-end
                 indent  %s"selector_ref:" SP string    line-end
                 indent  %s"roles:" line-end
                 1*reach-role

reach-role     = indent2 "- " %s"role:" SP symbol line-end
                 indent3 %s"grants:" line-end 1*reach-grant
                 [indent3 %s"limits:" line-end reach-limits]
                 [indent3 %s"never:" line-end 1*(indent4 "- " reach-action line-end)]

reach-grant    = indent4 "- " %s"repo:" SP reach-repo line-end
                 indent5 %s"access:" SP reach-access line-end
                 indent5 %s"actions:" line-end 1*(indent6 "- " reach-action line-end)
                 [indent5 %s"branch:" SP glob-pattern line-end]
                 [indent5 %s"paths:" line-end 1*(indent6 "- " glob-pattern line-end)]
                 [indent5 %s"max_files_per_push:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]

reach-access   = %s"read" / %s"write"

; close_pr and the grantable actions come before the never-only ones;
; spec rule 15 keeps the never-only actions out of grants.
reach-action   = %s"attach" / %s"push_branch" / %s"open_draft_pr"
               / %s"comment" / %s"close_pr" / %s"merge" / %s"force_push"
               / %s"delete_branch" / %s"change_environment"
               / %s"change_permissions" / %s"sign_commit"

; Each block is optional; spec rule 23 requires at least one field in
; a block that is present.
reach-limits   = [indent4 %s"window:" line-end
                    [indent5 %s"days:" line-end 1*(indent6 "- " weekday line-end)]
                    [indent5 %s"hours_utc:" SP 1*2DIGIT "-" 1*2DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"blackout:" line-end 1*(indent6 "- " day-range line-end)]
                    [indent5 %s"scope:" SP window-scope line-end]]
                 [indent4 %s"extent:" line-end
                    [indent5 %s"max_orgs:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"max_repos:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"spawn_depth:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"spawn_breadth:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]]
                 [indent4 %s"ttl:" line-end
                    [indent5 %s"wall_minutes:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"idle_minutes:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"max_tool_calls:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"max_attaches:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"max_pushes:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                    [indent5 %s"max_prs:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]]
                 [indent4 %s"rate:" line-end
                    indent5 %s"pushes_per_hour:" SP 1*DIGIT line-end]
                 [indent4 %s"on_breach:" SP breach-mode line-end]

weekday        = %s"mon" / %s"tue" / %s"wed" / %s"thu" / %s"fri"
               / %s"sat" / %s"sun"
window-scope   = %s"actions" / %s"all"
breach-mode    = %s"deny_and_report" / %s"deny_and_interrupt" / %s"deny"
calendar-date  = 4DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT
day-range      = calendar-date ".." calendar-date

; --- Primitives ----------------------------------------------------

indent         = "  "                    ; Exactly 2 spaces (not tabs)
indent2        = indent indent           ; Exactly 4 spaces
indent3        = indent indent indent    ; Exactly 6 spaces
indent4        = indent3 indent          ; Exactly 8 spaces
indent5        = indent4 indent          ; Exactly 10 spaces (v1.3.0)
indent6        = indent5 indent          ; Exactly 12 spaces (v1.3.0)

value          = string / symbol / bare-version
bare-version   = 1*DIGIT *("." 1*DIGIT)  ; e.g., 1.0.0, 2.3, 42

string         = DQUOTE *string-char DQUOTE
string-char    = %x20-21 / %x23-5B / %x5D-7E
               / UTF8-2 / UTF8-3 / UTF8-4
               / escape
escape         = "\" (DQUOTE / "\" / %s"n" / %s"t")

symbol         = ALPHA *(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / ".")
spdx-id        = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / ".")
repo-path      = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "/")
reach-repo     = reach-seg "/" reach-seg               ; exactly owner/name (rule 16)
reach-seg      = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_")
deed-filename  = deed-char deed-tail           ; 1*deed-char %s".deed", written
deed-tail      = deed-char deed-tail / %s".deed"  ; so a greedy parser can end
deed-char      = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "."  ; (2026-11-09 changelog note)
file-path      = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "/" / ".")
glob-pattern   = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "_" / "/" / "."
               / "*" / "?" / "[" / "]" / "{" / "}")

date           = iso8601-datetime                ; full RFC 3339 datetime, first:
               / 4DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT   ; or ISO 8601 calendar date
                                                 ; (see the 2026-11-09 changelog note)

iso8601-datetime = 4DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "T"
                   2DIGIT ":" 2DIGIT ":" 2DIGIT
                   ["." 1*DIGIT]
                   ("Z" / ("+" / "-") 2DIGIT ":" 2DIGIT)

; --- UTF-8 Support (RFC 3629) -------------------------------------

UTF8-2         = %xC2-DF UTF8-tail
UTF8-3         = %xE0 %xA0-BF UTF8-tail
               / %xE1-EC 2UTF8-tail
               / %xED %x80-9F UTF8-tail
               / %xEE-EF 2UTF8-tail
UTF8-4         = %xF0 %x90-BF 2UTF8-tail
               / %xF1-F3 3UTF8-tail
               / %xF4 %x80-8F 2UTF8-tail
UTF8-tail      = %x80-BF

text-char      = VCHAR / SP / UTF8-2 / UTF8-3 / UTF8-4

line-end       = CRLF / LF

; --- Notes ---------------------------------------------------------
;  1. Indentation is EXACTLY 2 spaces per level. Tabs are INVALID.
;  2. The magic number "K9!" MUST be the first line (no leading ws).
;  3. SPDX header MUST appear before the first section.
;  4. metadata, project, and invariants sections are REQUIRED.
;  5. Optional sections appear in fixed order; each at most once.
;  6. deed_ref links to a .deed file for typed identity.
;  7. Line endings may be CRLF or LF (mixing is permitted).
;  8. Blank lines and full-line "#" comments are permitted between
;     sections, not within them.
;  9. Strings support escape sequences: \" \\ \n \t
; 10. Bare version numbers (e.g., 1.0.0) are valid unquoted values.
